  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there a school in Ramagundam that runs the IB Diploma or Cambridge IGCSE?", answer: "None currently. Every school inside Ramagundam and Peddapalli district follows either the Telangana State Board or CBSE; the only school listed for the town, Kendriya Vidyalaya NTPC Ramagundam, serves power-station families on CBSE. Anyone connected to IB or IGCSE here is almost always boarding elsewhere, most often around Hyderabad, or has recently moved back from a posting where a child was already enrolled internationally." },
    { question: "With no local teacher for this syllabus, how do you actually find a suitable tutor?", answer: "By dropping the geography filter altogether. A shortlist gets built from the exact IB subject and level, or Cambridge and Edexcel code, a student is sitting, drawing on tutors from wherever in India they happen to teach that syllabus well, since almost none live within Peddapalli district. A no-cost trial lesson comes before any commitment, and the search continues if the first name doesn't click." },
    { question: "Is Ramagundam home tuition delivered online or in person?", answer: "Online only. Tutors visiting a family's house is something that happens only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. A Ramagundam lesson runs entirely over video, one to one, with a shared screen for working through problems together. It is genuine private tuition taken at home, just delivered through a laptop rather than a visitor at the door." },
    { question: "How much should I expect an IB or IGCSE tutor to charge?", answer: "Pricing depends on the subject, the level, how long each session runs, and how recently a tutor has actually taught that specific syllabus, and gets locked in for your pairing before the trial lesson begins. HL subjects at Diploma level generally cost more than IGCSE Core work. Since delivery is entirely online, no travel component gets added anywhere, and no long agreement is required." },
    { question: "Our family was posted to Ramagundam through NTPC or Singareni mid-year. Can our child keep the same syllabus going?", answer: "Yes, and this comes up frequently among transferred families. A tutor continues exactly where the previous school stopped, matching the same board, syllabus and level instead of substituting a generic course. This matters especially for IGCSE, since Cambridge and Edexcel differ enough in technique that the specific board a child studied before shapes how a tutor approaches the material." },
    { question: "Is it worth arranging a tutor purely for school holidays if my child boards elsewhere?", answer: "Often, yes, especially given that Ramagundam has nothing local to fall back on for IB or IGCSE. A tutor works from the boarding school's own syllabus and level, and sessions get timed around school breaks, or an agreed evening slot during term if the boarding school is comfortable with that." },
    { question: "Can I watch a tutor teach before I decide anything?", answer: "Yes, every arrangement opens with a no-cost trial lesson built around a genuine topic from your child's syllabus. Nothing is owed either way once it ends. A short plan for the following month arrives afterward, and you choose whether to continue, request adjustments, or ask for someone else entirely." },
    { question: "Can a tutor complete or rewrite parts of my child's Internal Assessment?", answer: "No, and that boundary is firm. A tutor helps shape a workable research question, explains what each assessment criterion is really rewarding, works through a data-collection plan, and gives direct feedback on drafts, but the writing itself stays entirely the student's. Anything beyond that breaches IB's own academic integrity rules." },
    { question: "What range of IB Diploma subjects does IB Gram actually cover?", answer: "The major groups a Diploma student is likely sitting: both Maths routes, Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation, at HL and SL, plus Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science, Theory of Knowledge and support for the Extended Essay." },
    { question: "What about MYP or PYP students, not just Diploma candidates?", answer: "The full continuum is covered, from PYP right through to DP. Younger MYP students get help with criterion-based analysis across sciences and languages, plus the Personal Project's process journal, while PYP support focuses on reading, writing, number confidence and the research skills an Exhibition project requires." },
    { question: "Can an online tutor really replace someone sitting next to my child?", answer: "In Ramagundam's case there is no real local, in-person alternative to compare against, since no specialist for a specific HL subject or Cambridge and Edexcel code lives nearby to begin with. A shared digital whiteboard, marked-up past papers and recorded explanations of worked problems together cover the same ground online, while giving access to specialists from across the country instead of settling for proximity." },
    { question: "How do you decide which tutors are good enough to introduce to a family?", answer: "Each one is checked against their qualifications, how recently they have taught the exact subject and level in question, and how well they understand the relevant assessment criteria, before a family ever meets them. Since Ramagundam has no local IB or IGCSE provision of its own, this check weighs recent, live-syllabus experience particularly heavily. The trial lesson then lets a family form their own judgement." },
    { question: "At what point should tutoring start for a child here?", answer: "Ideally at the start of the course itself, Class 11 for the Diploma or Grade 9 for either IGCSE board, which leaves time to fix gaps before internal assessments, deadlines and predicted grades all land close together. Starting later in the final year is still worthwhile, with effort concentrated on the topics and papers most likely to move a grade." },
    { question: "My child is moving over from SSC or CBSE. What should we expect to be different?", answer: "The content overlaps more than the question style does. IGCSE and IB command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' ask for a different shape of answer than an SSC or CBSE paper trains a student to give, and getting ahead of that, ideally a term before the switch, avoids the surprise showing up on a first graded piece of work." },
    { question: "Does scheduling account for Ramagundam's own routines, including shift work?", answer: "Yes. Weekday evenings and weekend mornings are the usual slots families choose, and timing takes NTPC and Singareni shift patterns into account where a parent's own hours shape the household schedule. Summer heat and the Bathukamma period both get worked around too, and a second weekly slot near mocks or exams is easy to add." },
    { question: "What if my child and the first tutor just don't get along?", answer: "Then a different tutor gets brought in. Check-ins happen with families on a regular few-week cycle exactly to catch this kind of mismatch quickly, rather than expecting a child to persevere regardless. There is no long-term contract in place, so a change of tutor, or a pause, costs nothing." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any formal relationship with NTPC, Singareni, a local school, or the exam boards themselves?", answer: "None. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no affiliation, endorsement or representation tied to NTPC, Singareni Collieries, any school mentioned on this page, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Schools are named solely to show, honestly, where confirmed IB and IGCSE provision exists nearest to Ramagundam." },
  ],

